.TH "ODIR-MOUNT" "7" "" "odir 25.1.2+onesimus.0.2.0" "Onesimus Director Commands"
.SH NAME
odir\-mount \- mount: Mount storage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
mount [storage=<storage>] [sd=<sd>] [<storage\-name>] [slot=<slot>] [drive=<drive>] [device=<device>] [jobid=<jobid>] [job=<job>] [ujobid=<ujobid>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Asks the Storage Daemon to use a device again: on tape drives to read the loaded tape and make it available to jobs, on autochangers to load a volume from a slot first (slot=). Needed after unmount, after inserting a tape, or when a job waits for a volume. It changes the device state in the Storage Daemon, not the catalog. File devices are always mounted.
.PP
The storage is given as storage=, sd= or by its bare name; without it a selection list appears. jobid=, job= or ujobid= use the storage of a running job. A keyword without a value is read as a storage name.
.PP
Onesimus deviation: a job waiting for a volume whose Job resource has no Max Wait Time is cancelled after 10 minutes (unlimited in Bareos). Until then mount or a newly labelled volume lets the job continue.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.SS "mount"
.TP
.B "storage=<storage>"
Storage name (name; values from .storages)
.TP
.B "sd=<sd>"
Storage name (as storage=) (name; values from .storages)
.TP
.B "<storage\-name>"
Storage name without key (positional value; values from .storages)
.TP
.B "slot=<slot>"
Slot (number)
.TP
.B "drive=<drive>"
Drive number (number)
.TP
.B "device=<device>"
Device name (text)
.TP
.B "jobid=<jobid>"
Storage of a job (number)
.TP
.B "job=<job>"
Storage of a job (name; values from .jobs)
.TP
.B "ujobid=<ujobid>"
Storage of a job (text)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B "mount storage=Autochanger slot=3 drive=0"
load slot 3 into drive 0 and mount it
.TP
.B "mount jobid=42"
mount the storage the running job 42 waits on
.SH ORIGIN
Bareos console command.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR odir\-commands (7),
.BR oconsole (1)
